      "writtenOn": "2025-05-19T23:41:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No strong opinion really. It doesn\u0027t have to be treated as a sentinel value, as any very large timeout will effectively do the same thing. (Actually in Wasm we\u0027re limited to a timeout of `INT32_MAX` ms \u003d 24.8 days so anything greater than that becomes infinite.)\n\nWe could provide a #define, it would avoid needing to remember the type of the timeout, and slightly help guide people toward the special-case paths in Dawn for `UINT64_MAX`.\n\nhttps://github.com/webgpu-native/webgpu-headers/issues/543",
      "parentUuid": "0be8e6c4_085bf919",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
